# v1.0.0-rc (BYTES OVER NAMES): these are BYTE-EXACT artefacts. A round whose whole subject is
# "what do the first bytes of this file say" cannot let git rewrite line endings inside them — and
# `junk_named_jpg.jpg` (PDF text, no NUL) and the generator would otherwise be auto-detected as
# text and CRLF-converted on checkout, so the committed fixture and the checked-out one would
# differ. Same reason as `crates/testdata/.gitattributes`.
* -text
